e to make do with celestial workings and supernal medicine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds more like Necrotech to me...<br /> <br /> But why not wyld shape your cat girls into existence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T05:25:22-07:00","id":1325945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beast of Bitter Oblivion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1325782-the-resplendent-cat-girl-generals#post1325782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I\u2019m looking for suggestions what kind of cat girl should represent each direction and what kind of panoply I should craft for them what to name them as well as whether I should give them any specific powers to counter corresponding dragon styles. I\u2019m not sure whether you can grant knowledge of martial art charms to beings you create that are equivalent to 2nd circles.<br /> Like For North like Maybe Lynx Girl or British Blue hair and if air is countering earth would she need a giant piercing weapon to counter earth soak ? Or should same element counter each other and give them resistance to anima flare if that element.<br /> <br /> All suggestions are welcome.<br /> <br /> P.S demons are bad mkay.</div> </div> </div> </div>Powerful creatures like that should be able to learn martial arts.<br /> <br /> For the creatures... for the East I'd suggest the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jaguar\" target=\"_blank\">Jaguar</a>, a medium-sized cat prevalent in tropical regions and notoriously aggressive (foling ambushes have a good chance of killing the mood for bigger cats like tigers. this one only gets angrier).<br /> For the South you can look at a bellicose variation of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sand_cat\" target=\"_blank\">Sand Cat</a>, or the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lion\" target=\"_blank\">Lion</a>. The former is pretty much the only true desert cat, a solitary small hunting chiefly rodents, but both belong in Creation's southern biomes.<br /> For the West, if you are hell-bent on a semi-aquatic or aquatic feline, there's the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fishing_cat\" target=\"_blank\">Fishing Cat</a>. If not, look at the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clouded_leopard\" target=\"_blank\">Clouded Leopard</a>. This one is an arboreal ambusher, jumping down on prey. Both are common in the forests around india and insular malaysia (my main reference for western climates).<br /> For the Blessed Isle, the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Andean_mountain_cat\" target=\"_blank\">Andean mountain cat</a> is probably very prominent around the imperial mountain, and thus famously recognized as part of the scenery for holy pilgrims.<br /> The North is probably filled with lynxes, of which the most chill is probably the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canada_lynx\" target=\"_blank\">canadian</a>.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 07-19-2019, 08:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T05:55:43-07:00","id":1325952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uknown DarkLord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1325782-the-resplendent-cat-girl-generals?p=1325943#post1325943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds more like Necrotech to me...<br /> <br /> But why not wyld shape your cat girls into existence?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t have wyld shaping also it may be more appropriate to make a race of Amazon cat girl warriors than guardian deities for which celestial workings are more appropriate power level wise. Also with his wits 1 and survival zero he probably get hopelessly lost in the tiniest of wyld zones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12796-beast-of-bitter-oblivion","name":"Beast of Bitter Oblivion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12796_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T07:00:40-07:00","id":1325970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beast of Bitter Oblivion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1325782-the-resplendent-cat-girl-generals#post1325782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like For North like Maybe Lynx Girl or British Blue hair.<br /> <br /> All suggestions are welcome.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not a British Blue Hair Lynx Girl? In Creation taxonomy is more inspiration guidelines than any sort of hard code or natural law. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beast of Bitter Oblivion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1325782-the-resplendent-cat-girl-generals?p=1325936#post1325936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why? Because they are not sexy cat girl war gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are if you make them to be - remember, elementals are <i>shaped</i>, not called, in 3rd edition. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 07-19-2019, 10:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T09:26:31-07:00","id":1326018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1325782-the-resplendent-cat-girl-generals?p=1325970#post1325970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why not a British Blue Hair Lynx Girl? In Creation taxonomy is more inspiration guidelines than any sort of hard code or natural law. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> They are if you make them to be - remember, elementals are <i>shaped</i>, not called, in 3rd edition. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Making them elementals would take me over my cap of 5 and get me slapped. I asked other players to slap me if I ever summoned more than 5 elementals. I already broke it once I don\u2019t want to encourage people to do it again . Also elementals only last a year at least with a working you invest part of your soul in them via XP they feel more special rather just summoning random mooks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12796,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12796-beast-of-bitter-oblivion","user":"Beast of Bitter Oblivion","dat